#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Side by side"
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Machines hand things to the machines they touch."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Watch the ore cross each gap."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "There are no belts. A machine hands what it makes to any orthogonal neighbour that wants it, and splits it evenly if several do. While you place one, the green tiles are where it would be fed and could hand its work on."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Every step pays more"
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Crushed ore sells for more than raw ore."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Two identical Drills. The lower line earns more."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Selling raw ore works and is never the best you can do. Each refining step trades throughput for value, and the trade is always worth making if you can keep the machine fed."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Helpers let things through"
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Heaters, Coolers and Boosters let things pass through them."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Ore crosses the Amplifier as if it were not there."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "A Boiler, Coolant Cell, Amplifier, Duplicator or Condenser makes nothing — but material passes straight through it, so it costs you a tile of production and never a connection. Put one inside a working line, not beside it."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Helpers boost what they touch"
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "The more machines a Booster touches, the more it helps."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "One Amplifier, four neighbours, all of them faster."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "The boost grows with how many working machines a support tile touches: one neighbour is face value, four is two and a half times that. Vaults do not count — there is no rate to raise. Move it one tile and the number on the preview changes before you buy."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "The lights show the problem"
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Green: working. Amber: nowhere to send it. Red: nothing coming in."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Amber on the left, red on the right."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Green is working. Amber means its output is backed up — look downstream. Red means it is not being fed — look upstream. The two point in opposite directions, so you can follow the colour to the culprit."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Heat can help"
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "A Smelter likes heat. Put a Boiler next to it."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "The Smelter is hot, and fast."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "A Smelter wants to be hot. A Boiler next to it gets it there. Every machine emits heat into its own tile and half of that into each neighbour."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Heat can hurt"
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Too much heat slows a Press down."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "The Press is choking on the Smelter's heat."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "A Press wants to be cold and sits next to things that are not. That is the puzzle: the same Boiler that pays for one tile costs you the next one."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Cooling"
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "A Coolant Cell cools the machines around it."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Same board, one Coolant Cell. The Press recovers."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "A Coolant Cell produces nothing. It buys back the throughput the heat was taking, and it costs you a tile you would rather have filled. That trade is most of the late game."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "The long chain"
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Ore, gravel, ingot, plate, part: one step at a time."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "One of everything, one tile each."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Each step takes one of the thing below it, so one supplier is enough. A full chain earns about what the same tiles of Drills and Crushers would — and it is the only thing that makes Components, which teach a Lab the most."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Research buys what lasts"
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "Labs turn materials into research. What it buys outlasts a collapse."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "The Lab earns no credits at all."
msgstr ""

#: res://scripts/ui/codex.gd
msgid "A Lab turns Ingots, Plates or Components into Research -- most from a Component -- and Research buys upgrades that outlast the shaft. A board with no Lab is a board with no future, and a board that is only Labs has no present."
msgstr ""

